":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"distress","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-07T05:43:41.920Z","evidenceHash":"36f4acd6a09b1a86f5c53c07268505e6834941637e62c6b11cd83696c59eebe2"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2026-08-02","period":"FY 2026","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-07T05:43:41.920Z","evidenceHash":"36f4acd6a09b1a86f5c53c07268505e6834941637e62c6b11cd83696c59eebe2"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/CPB.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/CPB.png","website":"https://www.thecampbellscompany.com","ceo":"Mick J. Beekhuizen","full_time_employees":"13500","description":"Campbell Soup Company (CPB) is a leading international producer and marketer of a wide variety of food and beverage products. The enterprise conducts its business through two main operational divisions: Meals & Beverages and Snacks. The Meals & Beverages segment serves both retail and food service industries throughout the United States and Canada. Its extensive product range includes classic Campbell's condensed and ready-to-enjoy soups; Swanson brand broths and stocks; Pacific Foods' line of broths, soups, and non-dairy beverages; Prego pasta sauces; Pace brand Mexican sauces; Campbell's gravies, pasta dishes, beans, and dinner sauces; Swanson canned poultry; Plum organic baby food and snacks; V8 juices and drinks; and Campbell's tomato juice. The Snacks division primarily targets the retail sector, with a significant presence in Latin America. This segment offers a diverse array of treats, such as Pepperidge Farm's selection of cookies, crackers, fresh bakery items, and frozen goods, including Milano cookies and Goldfish crackers. Other notable brands within this category are Snyder's of Hanover pretzels, Lance sandwich crackers, Cape Cod and Kettle Brand potato chips, Late July snacks, Snack Factory Pretzel Crisps, Pop Secret popcorn, Emerald nuts, and numerous other snacking options. Campbell Soup Company employs a comprehensive distribution strategy, selling its merchandise across an extensive network that encompasses major retail food chains, mass discounters and merchandisers, club stores, convenience stores, drug stores, and dollar stores. Additionally, products are available via e-commerce platforms, various other retail, commercial, and non-commercial establishments, and a system of independent contractor distributors. Established in 1869, the company's corporate headquarters are situated in Camden, New Jersey.","description_en":"Campbell Soup Company (CPB) is a leading international producer and marketer of a wide variety of food and beverage products. The enterprise conducts its business through two main operational divisions: Meals & Beverages and Snacks. The Meals & Beverages segment serves both retail and food service industries throughout the United States and Canada. Its extensive product range includes classic Campbell's condensed and ready-to-enjoy soups; Swanson brand broths and stocks; Pacific Foods' line of broths, soups, and non-dairy beverages; Prego pasta sauces; Pace brand Mexican sauces; Campbell's gravies, pasta dishes, beans, and dinner sauces; Swanson canned poultry; Plum organic baby food and snacks; V8 juices and drinks; and Campbell's tomato juice. The Snacks division primarily targets the retail sector, with a significant presence in Latin America. This segment offers a diverse array of treats, such as Pepperidge Farm's selection of cookies, crackers, fresh bakery items, and frozen goods, including Milano cookies and Goldfish crackers. Other notable brands within this category are Snyder's of Hanover pretzels, Lance sandwich crackers, Cape Cod and Kettle Brand potato chips, Late July snacks, Snack Factory Pretzel Crisps, Pop Secret popcorn, Emerald nuts, and numerous other snacking options. Campbell Soup Company employs a comprehensive distribution strategy, selling its merchandise across an extensive network that encompasses major retail food chains, mass discounters and merchandisers, club stores, convenience stores, drug stores, and dollar stores. Additionally, products are available via e-commerce platforms, various other retail, commercial, and non-commercial establishments, and a system of independent contractor distributors. Established in 1869, the company's corporate headquarters are situated in Camden, New Jersey.","description_zh":"Campbell Soup Company（美股代碼：CPB）為 Consumer Defensive 領域之重要企業，專注於 Packaged Foods 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"1 Campbell Place","city":"Camden","state":"NJ","zip":"08103-1799","country":"US","phone":"856 342 4800","full_address":"1 Campbell Place, Camden, NJ 08103-1799, US","range_52w":"18.6-32.04","year_high":32.04,"year_low":18.6,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":18.6,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-11-02","name":"Cunfer Todd E","title":"officer: EVP, Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"F-InKind","shares":7597,"price":21,"total_val":0.16},{"date":"2026-10-13","name":"Palumbo Kelly L","title":"officer: SVP, Controller and CAO","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":16161,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-13","name":"Nippert Melissa","title":"officer: SVP, Chief Transformation Ofcr","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":19709,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"Anand Mohit","title":"officer: EVP / President, Snacks","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":147060,"price":19.38,"total_val":2.85},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"Anand Mohit","title":"officer: EVP / President, Snacks","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":25227,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"Palumbo Kelly L","title":"officer: SVP, Controller and CAO","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":8619,"price":0,"total_